# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Q-Lock
#
# The vault section is the important part of this file. Everything else
# is routine.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── VAULT AND KEY MATERIAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One committed share file is a permanent leak. Git history is forever,
# and this repository may go public. Three shares reconstruct a key that
# controls a child's inheritance.
#
# CI enforces this too (scripts in .github/workflows/ci.yml), because a
# .gitignore only stops accidents — it does nothing about `git add -f`.

*_shares/
*_share_*.json
share_*.json
*_vault.json
nevaeh_xrpl_vault.json
nevaeh_nev369_vault.json
architect_vault.json
# Password-sealed wallets and the escrow's plaintext signing identity.
nev369_wallet*.json
qlock_attestation.json
keys.json
*.key
*.pem
*.seed

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# ── Rust ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/target
**/target/
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This is a workspace of binaries, not a
# published library, and the whole point is that the image CI builds
# resolves the same dependency graph that was tested. For a consensus
# binary that is not a preference — two nodes on different patch
# versions of a signature crate can disagree about validity and fork.
# Do not add Cargo.lock here.

# ── Node ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Foundry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# lib/ is installed by `forge install` (OpenZeppelin v5.0.2, forge-std).
# broadcast/ holds deployment receipts; keep your own copy, but they carry
# RPC URLs and deployer addresses you may not want public.

contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/lib/
contracts/broadcast/

# ── WASM build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

crates/godshield-wasm/pkg/

# ── Inheritance ceremony output ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# inheritance_record.json holds the OfferSequence — the one value without
# which the escrow can never be finished — plus the beneficiary's name and
# date of birth. Back it up in several places. None of them should be a
# public git repository.

inheritance_record*.json

# ── Chain and database data ────────────────────────────────────────────

chain.db/
*.sled
data/
pgdata/

# ── TLS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

nginx/certs/
!nginx/certs/.gitkeep

# ── Editors and OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Local scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.local
tmp/
scratch/

# Patch-script backups (contain a copy of .env)
.backup-*/
godshield_gateway.json

# Built on the server by scripts/build-downloads.sh
apps/downloads/

# ── Added by github_push.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything wallet- or key-shaped, anywhere in the tree.
*wallet*.json
*_attestation*.json
*gateway*.json
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# Chain databases, logs, archives, one-off update scripts.
*.db
*.sqlite*
*.log
*.zip
*.tar.gz
nginx/certbot/
/*_patch.sh
/qlock_*update*.sh
/qlock_server_mining.sh
/github_push.sh
.env.bak*

# Keypairs saved under any name or extension (qlock_attestation.js was
# committed once because only the .json name was listed).
*attestation*.json
*attestation*.js
*keypair*.json
*keypair*.js
test_wallet*
